{title: 281 - I Gave My Life for Thee}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #281 • WHITE • 12.12.15.15}
{lyricist: Frances Ridley Havergal}
{composer: J. E. White}
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 281}
{meta: tune WHITE}
{meta: meter 12.12.15.15}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Igave [Ab]my life [Db]for thee, [Ab]My precious blood [Fm]I shed,
[Eb]That [Ab]thou might'st ransom be, [Db]And quickened [Ab/Eb]from the [Eb7]dead;
[Ab]Igave, [Eb]I gave My life [Ab]for thee, What hast [Eb]thou given for Me?
[Ab]Igave, [Db]I gave My life for [Ab]thee, What [Eb]hast thou given for [Ab]Me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]My [Ab]Fathers house of [Fm]light,
[Eb]My [Ab]glory circled [Fm]throne,
[Eb]I [Ab]left for [Db]earthly [Ab/Eb]night,
[Eb]For [Ab]wanderings [Db]sad [Ab/Eb]and [Eb7]lone;
[Ab]I [Eb]left, I [Ab]left it [Eb]all for thee,
[Ab]Hast [Eb]thou left [Ab]aught [Eb]for Me?
[Ab]I [Db]left, I left [Ab]it [Eb]all for thee,
[Ab]Hast [Db]thou left [Ab]aught [Eb]for Me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]I [Ab]suffered much for [Fm]thee,
[Eb]more [Ab]than [Db]thy [Ab]tongue can [Fm]tell,
[Eb]Of [Ab]bitterest [Db]agony,
[Eb]To [Ab]rescue thee [Db]from [Ab/Eb]hell;
[Ab]I've [Eb]borne, I've [Ab]borne it [Eb]all for thee,
[Ab]What [Eb]hast thou [Ab]borne [Eb]for Me?
[Ab]I've [Db]borne, I've borne [Ab]it [Eb]all for thee,
[Ab]What [Db]hast thou [Ab]borne [Eb]for Me?
{end_of_verse}
